      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Following a 21-week double-blind trial that compared the effects of treatment with auranofin (AUR), gold sodium thiomalate, and placebo in 193 patients, 147 patients entered a 1-year, open-label study of treatment with AUR (6 mg/day). Results of this open-label study suggest that AUR has a long-term use profile similar to that of other slow-acting antirheumatic drugs. AUR appears to be capable of sustaining an initial response to gold sodium thiomalate. The withdrawal rate remains relatively high: Nearly half of the study patients had discontinued AUR by the end of 1 year."},
